EVTXtract by Willi Ballenthin was studied at fixed commit
0895be4c25125b5d087cc1c51b601e2852a67b85. Its selected complete runtime, CLI,
packaging entry, README and full Apache License 2.0 were reviewed. Original
authorship is retained; the applicant is not the original sole author of EVTXtract.
Its complete license is preserved in licenses/EVTXtract-Apache-2.0.txt.
EVTXtract code, lxml, hexdump, python-evtx and raw event fixtures are not shipped.

All ten previously independently written EvtxRecordReview runtime modules are
copied byte-for-byte into the private _record_core package at the published
commit c6b12c0497ee9e28d71c1322c5c01790011732f2. That prior Codex-assisted project
is credited rather than presented as newly invented in this recovery project.
Its independent fixture writer and 73 tests are reused here; test import targets
are adapted to the private package. Recovery-specific carving, catalog matching,
provenance decisions, bounded AST XML reconstruction and their tests are new.

The prior decoder was informed by python-evtx, copyright 2012, 2013 Willi
Ballenthin while at Mandiant, fixed commit
1edde3655c676bd44990ce9762d6b8f73334ed1d. Complete Apache License 2.0 is preserved
in licenses/python-evtx-Apache-2.0.txt. Its historical acknowledgement of Andreas
Schuster's EVTX format research and Parse-Evtx is retained; Parse-Evtx code was
not audited, copied, invoked or bundled. Microsoft MS-EVEN6 and libyal/libevtx
format references informed the prior finite decoder; their code/text is not
shipped or claimed as applicant authorship. The POSIX snapshot-reader pattern
is shared portfolio work, not a new original format algorithm.
